{{also|Auch}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|goh|ouh}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*auk}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|ook||also}}, {{cog|fy|ek||also, too}}, {{cog|lb|och||also}}, {{cog|sv|och||and}}, {{cog|is|og||and}}, and obsolete/archaic {{cog|en|eke||also}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/aʊ̯x/|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/aʊ̯/|lang=de}} {{a|chiefly southern Germany and Austria; also in the northern half in some positions, e.g. before ''{{l|de|nicht}}''}}
* {{audio|De-auch.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[also]], [[too]]
# [[even]] (in the sense of "including the extreme case of"; ''cf.'' [[Wikipedia:Early Modern English|Early Modern English]] cognate ''[[eke#Adverb|eke]]'')
#: ''auch wenn'' &mdash; even if
# [[really]]
# {{lb|de|rare|dated}} and [[so]]

